# Responsibilities

## Training.Domain

Contains only core business concepts.

Domain must never reference:

* Strava
* EF Core
* HttpClient
* AWS
* OpenAI
* Telegram
* OpenClaw

Domain represents training concepts only.

Examples:

```text
Athlete
TrainingProgram
Workout
WorkoutCategory
TrainingLoad
Fatigue
RecoveryStatus
Recommendation
Mesocycle
Microcycle
TrainingBlock
```

Domain contains:

* Entities
* Value Objects
* Enums
* Domain Services
* Domain Events

No infrastructure concerns.

---

## Training.Application

Contains use cases.

Examples:

```text
GetTodaysWorkout
RecordAthleteFeedback
GenerateDailyInsights
GenerateMesocycleInsights
GetFatigueStatus
GetAthleteDashboard
```

Application orchestrates:

* Domain
* Repositories
* External providers

Application never calls HttpClient directly.

Application communicates only through interfaces.

Examples:

```csharp
IActivityProvider
IAthleteProvider
IRecommendationEngine
ITrainingLoadCalculator
```

Application contains:

* Commands
* Queries
* Handlers
* Validators
* Application Services

No Strava-specific logic.

---

## Training.Infrastructure

Contains infrastructure concerns.

Examples:

```text
EF Core
Postgres
Redis
AWS Secrets Manager
Repositories
Caching
Background Jobs
```

Infrastructure implements interfaces defined in Application.

Examples:

```csharp
IAthleteRepository
IWorkoutRepository
IRecommendationRepository
```

Infrastructure never contains business logic.

---

## Training.Strava

Dedicated Strava integration project.

Purpose:

Translate Strava concepts into platform concepts.

Contains:

```text
Http Clients
OAuth Flows
Token Refresh
Request Models
Response Models
Provider Implementations
```

Examples:

```csharp
StravaClient
StravaOAuthService
StravaTokenService
StravaActivityProvider
StravaAthleteProvider
```

The Strava project exposes abstractions used by Application.

Example:

```csharp
public class StravaActivityProvider : IActivityProvider
{
}
```

The rest of the solution should not know that Strava exists.

---

## Training.Api

API layer only.

Responsibilities:

* Authentication
* Authorization
* Controllers
* Agent endpoints
* DTO mapping

No business logic.

Controllers should be thin.

Example:

```text
POST /api/agent/daily
POST /api/agent/mesocycle
GET /api/athletes/{id}/dashboard
GET /api/athletes/{id}/fatigue
```

---

# Agent Architecture

Agents are first-class citizens.

Agents are consumers of application use cases.

Agents never talk directly to Strava.

Agents never access repositories directly.

Agents communicate through Application.

---

## Daily Agent

Purpose:

Monitor athlete day-to-day.

Responsibilities:

* Fetch daily activities
* Categorise workouts
* Capture athlete feedback
* Track fatigue markers
* Track recovery markers
* Store observations
* Produce daily recommendations

Inputs:

```text
Strava activities
Athlete feedback
Historical training data
```

Outputs:

```text
Workout classification
Daily load
Recovery status
Daily recommendation
```

Examples:

```text
Easy Run
Recovery Run
Tempo Run
Intervals
Long Run
Strength Session
Rest Day
```

---

## Mesocycle Agent

Purpose:

Analyse medium-term trends.

Runs every 3 weeks.

Responsibilities:

* Aggregate daily agent observations
* Analyse trends
* Detect overtraining
* Detect undertraining
* Recommend recovery periods
* Recommend progression
* Recommend plan modifications

Inputs:

```text
Daily observations
Training load trends
Fatigue trends
Recovery trends
```

Outputs:

```text
Increase volume
Reduce volume
Recovery week
Maintain plan
Adjust intensity
```

